              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An observation of the training examples reveals the following transformation rule:\n\n1. The input grid is split into two 10\u00d710 subgrids by a vertical line of color 5 at column index 10:\n   - Left subgrid: columns 0 to 9\n   - Right subgrid: columns 11 to 20\n2. For each cell `(r, c)` in the resulting 10\u00d710 output grid, compare the corresponding cells in the left and right subgrids:\n   - If both the left and right cells contain a non-zero color: keep the original color.\n   - If only the left cell contains a non-zero color (absent in the right): set to color `2`.\n   - If only the right cell contains a non-zero color (absent in the left): set to color `1`.\n   - If neither contains a color: set to `0`.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid.",
